<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Korps Marechaussee te voet</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1890</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Korps Marechaussee te voet was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> colonial counter-insurgency force formed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aceh">Aceh</a> in 1890. Its small, mobile <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brigade">brigades</a> of Indonesian soldiers under Dutch officers, armed with carbines and the klewang sword, pursued <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrillas</a> through jungle and hills. Used by General van Heutsz to break Acehnese resistance, it became notorious for harsh reprisals, above all in the Gayo and Alas campaign of 1904.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/korps-marechaussee-te-voet.jpg" alt="Korps Marechaussee te voet" width="320" height="442" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jan Hoynck van Papendrecht · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Marechaussees_O.I._leger._1896.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
